          "content": "Based on `migrate_secrets.ps1`, the goal is:\n\n**Moving from one GitHub organization to another** — likely a company/team is migrating all their repositories from an old GitHub org to a new one (e.g. renaming the org, splitting orgs, or consolidating).\n\nThe challenge is that **secrets and variables don't move automatically** when you transfer repos between orgs. GitHub's API never exposes secret values, so you can't just read and copy them. This script solves that by:\n\n1. Using **Azure Key Vault as the source of truth** for secret values — meaning the team already stores their secrets in Key Vault, so the script can fetch the actual values from there and re-set them in the new org.\n\n2. For anything not in Key Vault — it flags it in a CSV report so someone can set it manually.\n\n3. It handles **all levels** (org, repo, environment) so nothing is missed.\n\n**In short:** The team is migrating their entire GitHub org setup to a new org, and this script automates the tedious part of recreating all secrets and variables across potentially dozens of repos and environments, while producing an audit trail of everything that was/wasn't migrated."
